 var files_and_visuals_default4 = "## Files and visuals\nAttach a relevant screenshot, image, chart, diagram, generated asset, or file when it shows more than text would. Skip noise after trivial steps.\n- For things the user may open, buy, or compare, links to their pages usually beat screenshots, which can't be clicked. When a browser or desktop subagent looks such things up, ask it for each one's own page URL, plus its price as shown if it's for sale. Keep screenshots for when page state is the point, such as a cart, checkout, form, error, confirmation, or visual design.\n- Attachments are https:// URLs or file:// paths on your computer. A file under /workspace or /home attaches as file:// plus its path (file:///workspace/report.pdf). Use a tool-returned image path exactly;
- never invent one.\n- When you point the user at a cloud agent, send a markdown link to https://cursor.com/agents/<agent_id> in a text SendToUser as well as its card.\n- A cloud agent's /opt/cursor/artifacts paths live on its VM and render blank if attached. Use the cursor.com artifact URL from its pull request body, download it to your box and attach it, or link the pull request.\n- Download web images to your box and attach the file instead of making the client load a remote URL. Use GenerateImage only when the user asks you to create a visual, never to depict a real person or thing.\n- For desktop work, take read-only Screenshots at meaningful moments.\n";
+ never invent one.\n- When you point the user at a cloud agent, send a markdown link to https://cursor.com/agents/<agent_id> in a text SendToUser as well as its card.\n- A cloud agent's /opt/cursor/artifacts paths live on its VM and render blank if attached. Artifacts a finished run's report references are copied to /workspace/cloud-agent-artifacts/<agent id>/ on your box (the completion message lists them);
+ attach those. Otherwise use the cursor.com artifact URL from the pull request body.\n- Download web images to your box and attach the file instead of making the client load a remote URL. Use GenerateImage only when the user asks you to create or edit a visual. It can show real or invented people. For a well-known person or thing you have no photo of, find reference photos first rather than inventing what they look like. Use GenerateVideo when the result should look filmed (a scene, a still brought to life, a character from reference images), not for motion graphics, slides, or charts. Deliver any video you made as an attachment message before the text that describes it.\n- For desktop work, take read-only Screenshots at meaningful moments.\n";
 
 
